    "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes both blocking review findings on PR #430 while preserving the three-tab mobile layout, existing renderer ownership, desktop presentation, and persistent stat-toast lifecycle.\n\n## Base, branch, and exact HEAD\n\n- Current main at reconciliation: `ceb999bb0c5c742c5fa5731d8d951f4a230fe21a` (after PRs #429, #428, and #427).\n- Branch: `codex/mobile-first-interface-redesign-20261014`.\n- Exact HEAD: `3ce2df634d4461c5d98870647cb41fc0566afed3`.\n- Reconciliation commit `6f846ca019491716ab0143a6704dc45a7328e46b` has parents old PR HEAD `f88e428d16b64c4628befa433e93ebcb2d3b8404` and current main `ceb999bb0c5c742c5fa5731d8d951f4a230fe21a`; the follow-up commit only removes an extra trailing blank line from mirrored entrypoints. The branch was advanced with an expected-SHA check and without force. No PR merge was performed.\n\n## Review fixes\n\n- Selected DM, Battles, and Events panels and their content bodies are displayed only when the renderer has not marked them `.hidden`. Tab selection leaves renderer state untouched.\n- A long press on a points or REP icon now prefers an active ancestor `data-stat-cap-hint`. The actual touched icon remains the tooltip's `aria-describedby` owner.\n- Desktop hint behavior, game state/economy, the existing toast lifecycle, and Web/docs mirror ownership are unchanged.\n\n## Changed files\n\n- `AsyncScene/Web/index.html`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/mobile-ui.css`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-mobile.js`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-dm.js`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-battles.js`\n- `AsyncScene/Web/ui/ui-events.js`\n- `docs/index.html`\n- `docs/ui/mobile-ui.css`\n- `docs/ui/ui-core.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-mobile.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-dm.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-battles.js`\n- `docs/ui/ui-events.js`\n- `tools/serve_mobile_interface_test.py`\n- `tools/test_mobile_first_interface.html`\n- `tools/test_mobile_first_interface_contract.py`\n\nThe only overlap with changes made on main since the original PR base was the two entrypoint files. Their latest main cache-buster updates were retained and combined with the mobile tab markup and wiring. The compare against current main contains exactly the 17 paths listed above.\n\n## Executed checks\n\n- `python3 -m unittest tools/test_mobile_first_interface_contract.py -v`: PASS, 11 tests.\n- Stage 6 hint/toast regressions: PASS (11 tests); persistent-toast regression: PASS; five-profile runtime regressions: PASS (7 tests).\n- Stage 7.15 boot mirror and visible-first-event checks: PASS.\n- `node --check` for changed UI JavaScript modules: PASS.\n- Web/docs byte parity for the seven paired mobile runtime/entrypoint files: PASS.\n- `git diff --check`: PASS on the isolated changed-path snapshot.\n- Built-in Codex Browser ran `tools/test_mobile_first_interface.html` at 390×844. The output passed fresh/closed/open/closed DM, hidden Battles and Events bodies, tab-state and renderer preservation, both swipe directions and edge stops, vertical scroll, button protection, divider drag/keyboard, short tap and long press, points/REP cap-message priority and touched-icon ARIA ownership, persistent toasts, 320×568 narrow, 844×390 landscape, 390×420 keyboard-height layout/recovery, desktop breakpoint, and mobile viewport restoration. The regression ran on a clean localhost origin against the updated main entrypoint and the unchanged current-main game renderers.\n\n## Browser and runtime limits\n\nCodex Browser generated touch PointerEvents and viewport-size changes. It does not reproduce physical iPhone touch hardware, iOS Safari, or the native iPhone keyboard. No Safari PASS is claimed.\n\n## GitHub CI\n\nRequired checks for exact HEAD `3ce2df634d4461c5d98870647cb41fc0566afed3` completed successfully:\n\n- `telemetry-receiver-checks` run [38535928060](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/38535928060): SUCCESS.\n- `ai-forensics-evidence` run [38535928062](https://github.com/samuray-games/AsyncScene/actions/runs/38535928062): SUCCESS.",
